<title>UK: BASF SEES KNOLL UNIT LOSSES CONTINUING.</title>
<headline>BASF SEES KNOLL UNIT LOSSES CONTINUING.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group BASF said on Thursday it expected losses at its Knoll AG unit to continue in the short term.  </p>
<p>&quot;Knoll has to bear a large part of the research and development costs and that is why the results are disappointing,&quot; said chairman Juergen Strube.</p>
<p>&quot;We cannot see this being readily addressed,&quot; He added. &quot;We see some improvement but not a positive prodit contribution.&quot;</p>
<p>Knoll AG is part of BASF pharamaceutical division.</p>
<p>BASF earlier reported a 5.8 percent rise in first half pretax profit to 2.458 billion marks.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
